 * ---
 *
 * ## Development Workflow
 *
 * @image html developer-workflow.svg "Development Workflow" width=45%
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Step-by-Step: Fork → Branch → PR
 *
 * @image html contribution-workflow.svg "Contributor Journey" width=45%
 *
 * **1. Fork** the repository on Codeberg.
 *
 * **2. Clone your fork:**
 * @code{.sh}
 * git clone https://codeberg.org/your-username/PicoKernel.git
 * cd PicoKernel
 * git submodule update --init --recursive
 * @endcode
 *
 * **3. Branch from `dev` never from `main`:**
 * @code{.sh}
 * git checkout dev
 * git pull origin dev
 * git checkout -b feat/layer-initial/your-feature
 * @endcode
 *
 * See @ref git_workflow for the full branch naming convention.
 *
 * **4. Implement, test, and document.**
 *
 * All three are required. Code that compiles but has no tests and no
 * documentation will be returned for revision.
 *
 * - Coding standards: @ref coding_style
 * - Documentation standards: @ref docs_style
 * - Architecture rules: @ref arch_overview
 *
 * **5. Open a Pull Request targeting `dev`.**
 *
 * Fill all PR fields: title, summary, and test evidence.
 * An empty PR description will be returned for revision without review.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## PR Checklist
 *
 * Before opening a Pull Request, confirm **all** of the following:
 *
 * - [ ] Branch targets `dev`, not `main`
 * - [ ] Branch name follows the naming convention (see @ref git_workflow)
 * - [ ] Code compiles cleanly: `cmake --build build`
 * - [ ] No architecture violations (see @ref arch_overview rule list)
 * - [ ] All public functions have complete Doxygen headers (see @ref docs_style)
 * - [ ] SPDX + file header block present on every modified `.c` and `.h`
 * - [ ] No debug output outside `#ifdef KERNEL_DEBUG`
 * - [ ] No direct hardware register access outside drivers
 * - [ ] PR title, summary, and test evidence fields are filled
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Review Process
 *
 * PRs require at least one maintainer review before merge.
 *
 * ### Reviewers check
 *
 * | Area | What is verified |
 * |------|-----------------|
 * | **Architecture** | No layer violations, kernel is the hub |
 * | **Documentation** | Complete Doxygen headers, no undocumented public APIs |
 * | **Correctness** | Logic is sound, error paths are explicit |
 * | **Security** | Debug gates present, no unchecked pointer arithmetic |
 * | **Style** | Naming, formatting, and comment conventions followed |
 *
 * ### On requested changes
 *
 * Requested changes must be addressed before merge. Push back on feedback you
 * disagree with - but back it up with reasoning. Disagreement handled in
 * comments leads to a better codebase. Unaddressed feedback leads to no merge.
 *
 * ---
 *
 * ## Finding Work
 *
 * | Resource | Purpose |
 * |----------|---------|
 * | [Codeberg Issues](https://codeberg.org/PicoKernel/PicoKernel/issues) | All open work items |
 * | [Codeberg Milestones](https://codeberg.org/PicoKernel/PicoKernel/milestones) | Milestone-scoped work |
 * | @ref milestones "Milestones & Roadmap" | Planned subsystems and deliverables |
 *
 * @attention Always check that an issue is unassigned and not already in progress
 * before starting work. Comment on the issue and ask it be assigned to you.
 *
